<overview>
<p>The CCAF fields conventional infantry in larger numbers than its limited industrial base might suggest, drawing on the Confederation's deep tradition of citizens' militia service. Capellan soldiers learn to fight with fewer resources and less support than their counterparts in wealthier states, compensating with resourcefulness and ideological commitment. CCAF foot platoons anchor the Confederation's garrison network, holding worlds that BattleMech forces cannot permanently occupy. Slow and vulnerable in open terrain, they depend on prepared positions and local knowledge to offset their lack of mobility. Equipped with combat shotguns and sonic stunners, these formations specialize in crowd control and civil suppression operations, balancing less-lethal compliance tools with lethal backup weapons.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date based on start date of Capellan Confederation faction
